    {
      "body": "Gentle ping on this one — it's been quiet for 17 days since the last activity, so I wanted to check whether there's anything else you'd like me to adjust or add before this can move forward. Happy to make changes if so. Thanks!",
      "created_at": "2026-09-27T22:05:45Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/hiyouga/LlamaFactory/pull/10828#issuecomment-5860257160",
      "id": 5860257160,
      "updated_at": "2026-09-27T22:05:45Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "li-lizhe"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "@hiyouga @codemayq — would one of you be able to take a look at this when you have a moment?\n\nThe change is confined to `src/llamafactory/model/model_utils/longlora.py`: the device-type check only compared against `\"cuda\"`, so the longlora path skipped its own handling on other accelerators. It now treats any non-CPU device the same way. One file, no behaviour change on CUDA.\n\nHappy to adjust anything if the approach doesn't fit how you'd like this handled.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-31T13:01:04Z",
